# Optional: LiteLLM / Gemini and other app env (brain reads MCP URLs from mcp.json).
# Copy to .env and adjust; docker-compose merges this with .env for the brain service.
#
# Local brain (`make agent-dev`): ``mcp.json`` uses Docker hostnames (``duckdb-mcp``, …). The process
# automatically rewrites those to ``127.0.0.1:8040`` / ``8043`` / ``8044`` when **not** inside a container.
# Set MCP_DISABLE_HOST_URL_REWRITE=1 to disable. MCP stack must publish those ports: ``make mcp-up``.
#
# Stacks: run ``infra/object-storage``, ``infra/duckdb``, and ``infra/dagster`` compose (MCP services included), then root ``docker-compose.yaml`` (brain).
# Both use Docker network `datacyber_mcp`.
#
# LLM backend (default: litellm):
#   MODEL_PROVIDER=litellm   # requires LITELLM_* + CHAT_MODEL (must match LiteLLM GET /v1/models).
#   MODEL_PROVIDER=openrouter   # requires OPENROUTER_API_KEY + CHAT_MODEL (OpenRouter slug, see https://openrouter.ai/models).
#                               # Optional: OPENROUTER_BASE_URL (default https://openrouter.ai/api/v1), OPENROUTER_HTTP_REFERER, OPENROUTER_APP_TITLE.
#   MODEL_PROVIDER=gemini    # requires GEMINI_API_KEY (or GOOGLE_API_KEY); CHAT_MODEL optional (defaults to gemini-2.0-flash).
#
# CHAT_MODEL is required for LiteLLM mode (no default — must match GET /v1/models exactly).
# Example virtual-key routes (your proxy must expose these ids):
#   local/gemini-3-flash-preview
#   local/gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview
#   local/gemini-3.1-pro-preview
# Wrong id (common typo): local/gemini-3-pro-preview — not the same as local/gemini-3.1-pro-preview.
#
# DATACYBER_PIPELINE_DEBUG=1   # brain: include structured debug in POST /agent/chat JSON (see docs/PIPELINE_AND_DEBUG.md)
#
# DuckDB Local UI (optional; compose profile `ui` — not started by default).
# From repo root, bring up MCP stack **and** duckdb-ui:
#   docker compose -f infra/duckdb/docker-compose.yaml --profile ui up -d
# Or: COMPOSE_PROFILES=ui docker compose -f infra/duckdb/docker-compose.yaml up -d
# Then open http://127.0.0.1:4213 (host :4213 → container :4214 → DuckDB on 127.0.0.1:4213).
# Override host port: DUCKDB_UI_PUBLISH_PORT=84213  DUCKDB_UI_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:84213
# DUCKDB_UI_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4213
#
# Langfuse (optional): tracing for POST /agent/chat when LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY and LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY are set.
#
# The brain sends data two ways (same keys for both):
#   1) Langfuse Python SDK — LANGFUSE_BASE_URL (HTTP API for spans, CallbackHandler, flush).
#   2) OpenTelemetry OTLP — OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT + Basic auth built from the keys in agent/utils/otel_tracing.py
#      (must point at Langfuse ingest, e.g. .../api/public/otel — see Langfuse self-host OTEL docs).
#
# Langfuse UI on the host at http://localhost:3000/:
#   • Brain on the host (`make agent-dev`): use loopback for both, e.g.
#       LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
#       OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/public/otel
#     Do not use `langfuse-web` — that name exists only on Langfuse’s Docker network.
#   • Brain in Docker (`docker compose up` root stack): `localhost:3000` is the *container* loopback, not your Mac.
#       Use http://host.docker.internal:3000 for LANGFUSE_BASE_URL and the same host for OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
#       (brain service has `extra_hosts: host.docker.internal:host-gateway`).
#   • LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=http://langfuse-web:3000 only works if this brain container shares Docker DNS with the Langfuse
#     compose project (attach both stacks to the same network). The default root compose does **not** attach to Langfuse.
#
# Cloud: LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=https://cloud.langfuse.com (or us.cloud.langfuse.com).
# Optional HTTP headers: X-Langfuse-Session-Id, X-Langfuse-User-Id (sessions / users in Langfuse UI).
#
# Jupyter (root `docker-compose.yaml` service `jupyter`):
#   JUPYTER_TOKEN=…           # Lab login; leave unset to print a random token in container logs.
#   VITE_JUPYTER_URL=http://localhost:8888   # Browser URL for embedded iframe (ui build arg).
#   VITE_JUPYTER_TOKEN=…      # Optional; same as JUPYTER_TOKEN for auto-login in iframe (exposed in UI JS).
